				1
			],
			"Message": "chore(Land): Sync Element submodule to streamline Sky bridge initialization\n\nUpdate the Element git submodule from `1a736c21` to `7adf09f0` to synchronize the latest stabilization of the editor's extension bridge layer.\n\nThe update syncs the Sky submodule to remove aggressive retry logic and polling loops found in `InstallInlineCompletions`, `InstallScm`, `InstallSearch`, and `InstallTreeView`. These complex mechanisms, designed to handle upstream instability, are replaced with direct service acquisition and synchronous execution. This change assumes the workbench bootstrap sequence is now stable, allowing bridge layers to register features immediately.\n\nThis simplification reduces bundle size, eliminates hidden asynchronous delays during feature activation, and ensures bridge logic remains strictly deterministic. Failed registrations now fail fast, making error tracking more transparent.",
			"SHA": "ab9cf5ffec7027c307ceaa09cd78c3c0de2e3f7b"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-23T08:09:37Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				133,
				1
			],
			"Message": "chore(Land): Sync Element submodule for Sky diagnostic bridge refinement\n\nUpdate the Element git submodule from `8fe235bf` to `1a736c21` to revert brittle forced-initialization logic in the diagnostic bridge and align with the reactive data-driven model.\n\nThe update syncs the Sky submodule to replace the previous implementation in `InstallDiagnostics.ts`, which forcibly opened the Problems panel on every diagnostic batch. This change removes all `openView` calls, throttling mechanisms, and per-batch visibility checks.\n\nThe new implementation relies on `IMarkerService.changeOne` for state updates and allows `MarkersView` to manage visibility naturally. A single, one-time intervention is introduced to clear persisted `activeFile` filters if the panel is already visible upon diagnostic arrival. This resolves the \"count shows but panel empty\" issue caused by stale filters without forcing UI state changes.\n\nThese updates reduce IPC overhead, eliminate unnecessary side effects, and ensure diagnostic updates strictly follow the reactive lifecycle of the editor UI.",
			"SHA": "0035fccf8743954dd5d67dda3331b22b7bd7a28b"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-23T08:01:39Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				133,
				1
			],
			"Message": "chore(Land): Sync Element submodule for stability refinements\n\nUpdate the `Element` git submodule from `deb49bcb` to `8fe235bf` to apply targeted stability fixes within the editor ecosystem.\n\nThis sync follows the previous major IPC alignment and error propagation update, addressing residual issues in the extension host (Cocoon) and native backend (Mountain) to ensure consistent behavior during extension loading and file system operations.\n\nSpecific changes include:\n- **Cocoon:** Refine task scheduling logic to prevent race conditions during the initialization of new language server protocols.\n- **Mountain:** Correct a minor edge case in `CacheBlob` serialization that could lead to transient state mismatches under high-load file system activity.\n- **Sky:** Optimize the cleanup of temporary webview containers to reduce memory pressure during rapid view switching.\n\nThese updates further solidify the IPC contract and ensure a stable runtime environment for the extension host and UI layers.",
			"SHA": "0898e1fa5d0437ca21b7928be8a302ccc0e96132"
		}
